# Independent parent preservation review

Reviewed merge `e197528820ab7cfb429e21259000957370abf1c6`, whose actual parents are integration `b51b0c0382a13a72854860ae17d7798f0875e4ee` and Task 1.3 `dc6b2005516327dbe7b5bfd05ef8da4c3b0c6f05`. Read-only review; evidence files are untracked. This sub-review did not rerun the heavy suites; the coordinating verifier owns those results.

## Findings

No actionable finding in merge preservation, grammar test relocation, manifest regeneration, or the changed current documentation.

## Parent source and test preservation

`compare_parents.py` obtains each parent's tracked blob IDs with `git ls-tree -r`, compares their final IDs, extracts Python test function names with AST, and extracts Rust `#[test]` names. `summary.json` and `tests-{HEAD,b51b0c0,dc6b200}.json` preserve the inventory. Function counts are source inventory counts, not expanded pytest or cargo execution counts.

- Integration has 157 pre-existing Python/config/trainer/test paths byte-identical in the merge. The only change within that scoped pre-existing set is the expected additive `python/owl/rs.pyi` observation binding. Thus all Task 3.x registration, training, evaluation, configs, startup guards, telemetry, compile guards and tests remain byte-for-byte from integration.
- In particular, `python/owl/model/compile_gemm.py` and all three compile-entry routes remain intact. The locked claim at lines 220–243 still checks the stack, sets `COMPILED_GEMM_BACKENDS` (`"ATEN"`), rejects another game's claim, and retains the per-call backend check at lines 247–256. Both direct model compile entries and configured `mlp` routing are unchanged.
- All Task 1.3 native observation/oracle/buffer files, root Cargo metadata, added Python binding and tests, trim checker/tests, and engine trim manifest are byte-identical to approved Task 1.3 `dc6b200`. No path was removed from that parent and no test function from that parent was lost.
- The only integration paths deleted are `engine_rs/tests/grammar_kernel.rs` (relocated) and the one-line `src/kaggriculture.rs` (replaced by `src/kaggriculture/mod.rs`, retaining `pub mod grammar`).
